{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012wzBm9TdpaJeVZUw6CkTUD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Gandalf (core) â€” Master Plan (Crucible Stage 1, re-scoped 2026-06-20)\n2\t\n3\t> NORTH STAR (RE-SCOPED to the researched, vetted core): Given any artifact, Gandalf produces a rigorous,\n4\t> TYPE-APPROPRIATE DIAGNOSIS of what is actually going on, what matters, and what is wrong or missing â€”\n5\t> ranked by consequence, resistant to sycophancy and false rigor, span-anchored and reasoning-before-verdict,\n6\t> and able to correctly return \"this is sound.\" It collects unverifiable factual claims as a\n7\t> needs_verification HANDOFF (it does NOT itself research).\n8\t\n9\t> WHY re-scoped: the Stage-1 Shark Tank found the expanded SITUATE+ELEVATE \"magic\" scope un-researched, over-\n10\t> lapping Crucible/Jumper/researchPrime, and resting on an unsolved vetting-vs-boldness tension. Per the trio's\n11\t> own \"build on vetted ground\" principle, the magic is DEFERRED to a compositional \"Gandalf-Advisor\" skill\n12\t> (own research+crucible cycle; see C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\planning\\portfolio-program\\crucible\\PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md). THIS\n13\t> plan is the vetted DIAGNOSE core â€” the review engine later cycles depend on. Method = the researched,\n14\t> adversarially-derived v2 protocol (`..\\research\\FINDINGS-and-PROTOCOL.md` PROTOCOL v2).\n15\t\n16\tPersona tier = TOP (Fable 5). Compositional advisor features are OUT of scope here.\n17\t\n18\t## North-Star criteria (inclusion test)\n19\t- **G1 DIAGNOSE:** type-appropriate, consequence-ranked, span-anchored, reasoning-before-verdict, can return \"sound.\"\n20\t- **G2 ANTI-SYCOPHANCY/FALSE-RIGOR:** the operator-wrong pass + forcing functions (â‰¥1 verdict-inverting hypothesis; named disconfirmation-or-\"none found\"); structural forcing, not bias-naming; no checklist-theater.\n21\t- **G3 TYPE-AWARE + RIGHT-SIZED:** triage depth (LIGHT/FULL) + artifact-type dispatch (argument/data/code; plan â†’ diagnostic read but route refutation-to-convergence to Crucible).\n22\t- **G4 SCOPE-HONEST:** unverifiable factual claims â†’ needs_verification handoff; NEVER self-assigns CORROBORATED/OBSERVED; NOT a rewriter; NOT the Shark Tank (must be able to emit zero defects + a populated what-matters).\n23\t- **G5 TESTABLE:** deterministic canaries incl. planted-defect fixtures per type + a SOUND fixture (anti-confabulation), scored by rubric/tolerance + A/B vs a generic \"review this\" baseline (must beat on must-find recall).\n24\t\n25\t## The protocol (v2 â€” the SKILL.md spec)\n26\tTRIAGE (right-size + type) â†’ FRAME deep-structure (classify by principle/mechanism, name the central claim +\n27\tthe interpretive frame) â†’ TYPE-APPROPRIATE LENS (argument: unstated warrant/backing/qualifier/rebuttal; data:\n28\tprovenance/sampling-bias/leakage/missingness/distribution/confounds; code: control-flow/invariants/edge-cases/\n29\terror-handling/concurrency/resource-lifecycle; plan: assumptions/deps â€” or hand to Crucible) â†’ CROSS-CUTTING\n30\tDIAGNOSIS with FORCING FUNCTIONS (D1 widen to â‰¥N readings incl. â‰¥1 verdict-INVERTING; D2 disconfirm â€” name\n31\tspecific inconsistent evidence or explicit \"none found\"; D3 events-vs-structure ONLY if a system) â†’\n32\tOPERATOR-WRONG PASS (â‰¥1 finding against the operator's evident preference, or justified absence; reason BEFORE\n33\tverdict) â†’ THREE-CHANNEL REPORT: WHAT'S-GOING-ON, WHAT-MATTERS, WHAT'S-WRONG (load_bearing ranked list â‰¥0;\n34\tmerged flip-test/premortem consequence gate) â†’ SCOPE-HONEST EVIDENCE (each factual finding internally-supported\n35\t| asserted-by-artifact | NEEDS-VERIFICATION â†’ handoff).\n36\t\n37\t### Committed output schema (lock field types in Stage 2)\n38\t`{ artifact_type, depth, frame, whats_going_on, what_matters[], load_bearing[]{issue,why,flip_test} (â‰¥0),\n39\tfindings[]{id,channel,type,location_span,severity_enum,confidence,evidence,suggested_action,blocks?},\n40\toperator_wrong_pass{found[]|justified_absence}, needs_verification[], what_would_change_my_conclusion,\n41\tresidual_uncertainty }`\n42\t\n43\t### Machine-checkable non-goals\n44\tNOT a rewriter (schema = analysis, not replacement); NOT the Shark Tank (MUST be able to emit zero Channel-2\n45\tdefects + populated what-matters â€” a \"sound\" verdict is valid); NOT researchPrime (no self-CORROBORATED;\n46\tunverifiable â†’ needs_verification); every finding has a non-empty location_span; reasoning precedes verdict;\n47\tload_bearing is a ranked list â‰¥0 (NOT pinned to 1); MUST emit what_would_change_my_conclusion +\n48\tresidual_uncertainty; nitpicks capped per depth; operator_wrong_pass present (found[] or justified_absence);\n49\ta \"sound/pass\" verdict REQUIRES populated what-matters (no empty flattery).\n50\t\n51\t## Canary design (deterministic, for the done-floor; G5)\n52\tPlanted-defect fixtures per type (argument: unstated-warrant gap + load-bearing flaw; data: leakage/missingness;\n53\tcode: inserted bug; plan: fatal assumption) with must-find oracles + A/B vs generic baseline; PLUS a SOUND\n54\tfixture (oracle: zero load-bearing + populated what-matters) to catch defect-confabulation. Rubric/tolerance\n55\tscored (stateless â‡’ non-deterministic), run-count for significance set at Stage 2.\n56\t\n57\t## Out of scope (anti-drift)\n58\tSITUATE (commission researchPrime) and ELEVATE (foresight + vetted value-adding suggestions) â€” DEFERRED to the\n59\tcompositional Gandalf-Advisor skill. NOT a rewriter; does not reimplement researchPrime/Jumper/Crucible.\n60\t\n61\t## Residual decisions for Stage 2 (pre-registration)\n62\tN (hypothesis count), nitpick cap, LIGHT/FULL depth thresholds, the canary pass-bar vs generic baseline + the\n63\trun-count for significance, committed schema field types, the operator-wrong-pass scoring rubric.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba2d1ee5-0a15-41ff-beda-07fd1f12224d","uuid":"1002ff6b-203b-43f6-9dfa-647efbd